<article class="env-definition" id="00MV">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00MV">Definition <span data-tag="00MV">10.102.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Suppose that $\varphi : R^ m \to R^ n$ is a map of finite free modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>rank</em> of $\varphi $ is the maximal $r$ such that $\wedge ^ r \varphi : \wedge ^ r R^ m \to \wedge ^ r R^ n$ is nonzero. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We let $I(\varphi ) \subset R$ be the ideal generated by the $r \times r$ minors of the matrix of $\varphi $, where $r$ is the rank as defined above. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>